{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"RLSA-2026:102219","published":"2026-11-25T06:02:32.309786Z","modified":"2026-11-25T06:30:02.492489986Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-64487","CVE-2026-72084","CVE-2026-74394","CVE-2026-90294","CVE-2026-90413","CVE-2026-90414","CVE-2026-92508","CVE-2026-92511","CVE-2026-93054","CVE-2026-98549","CVE-2026-99235","CVE-2026-99288","CVE-2026-99661"],"summary":"Important: kernel-rt security, bug fix, and enhancement update","details":"The kernel-rt packages provide the Real Time Linux Kernel, which enables fine-tuning for systems with extremely high determinism requirements.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: ALSA: caiaq: fix out-of-bounds read in the Traktor Kontrol S4 input parser (CVE-2026-64487)\n\n* kernel: scsi: target: Bound PR-OUT TransportID parsing to the received buffer (CVE-2026-72084)\n\n* kernel: RDMA/srpt: fix integer overflow in immediate data length check (CVE-2026-74394)\n\n* kernel: RDMA/core: Fix potential use after free in ib_free_cq() (CVE-2026-92508)\n\n* kernel: uio: Fix stale info pointer in failed registration path (CVE-2026-93054)\n\n* kernel: RDMA/core: Fix potential use after free in ib_destroy_cq_user() (CVE-2026-92511)\n\n* kernel: IB/isert: reject login PDUs declaring more data than was received (CVE-2026-90413)\n\n* kernel: IB/isert: reject PDUs declaring more data than was received (CVE-2026-90414)\n\n* kernel: IB/isert: delay the final Login Response until the session is registered (CVE-2026-90294)\n\n* kernel: tcp: prevent collapsing skbs across boundary in rtx queue (CVE-2026-98549)\n\n* kernel: kernel: Privilege escalation via use-after-free in event tracing subsystem (CVE-2026-99235)\n\n* kernel: kernel: Denial of Service via race condition in TCP socket lookup (CVE-2026-99288)\n\n* kernel: kernel: Memory corruption via integer overflow in GUP-fast (CVE-2026-99661)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* [Rocky Linux-8.10.z] RDMA/ulps: Backport security fixes (JIRA:Rocky Linux-289994)\n\n* [Rocky Linux-8.10.z] RDMA: Backport security fixes (JIRA:Rocky Linux-296076)\n\n* [Rocky Linux 8.10] Incorrect swap size value in /proc/swaps if swap area is very big (JIRA:Rocky Linux-302561)\n\n* lockd: fix vfs_test_lock() calls (JIRA:Rocky Linux-304667)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"kernel-rt","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:8","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/kernel-rt?distro=rocky-linux-8&epoch=0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0:4.18.0-553.189.1.rt7.530.el8_10"}],"database_specific":{"yum_repository":"NFV"}}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://storage.googleapis.com/resf-osv-data/RLSA-2026:102219.json"}},{"package":{"name":"kernel-rt-core","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:8","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/kernel-rt-core?distro=rocky-linux-8&epoch=0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0:4.18.0-553.189.1.rt7.530.el8_10"}],"database_specific":{"yum_repository":"NFV"}}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://storage.googleapis.com/resf-osv-data/RLSA-2026:102219.json"}},{"package":{"name":"kernel-rt-debug","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:8","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/kernel-rt-debug?distro=rocky-linux-8&epoch=0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0:4.18.0-553.189.1.rt7.530.el8_10"}],"database_specific":{"yum_repository":"NFV"}}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://storage.googleapis.com/resf-osv-data/RLSA-2026:102219.json"}},{"package":{"name":"kernel-rt-debug-core","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:8","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/kernel-rt-debug-core?distro=rocky-linux-8&epoch=0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0:4.18.0-553.189.1.rt7.530.el8_10"}],"database_specific":{"yum_repository":"NFV"}}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://storage.googleapis.com/resf-osv-data/RLSA-2026:102